**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests`

**How to implement.** The per-entry decision table of 001 §B as pure Domain data and functions (001 §B 'Per-entry import decision'; .spec-md §3.7, §5 `CatalogueImport`, `ImportDecision`; the S3.1 brief). No seam, store or caller changes in this step. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `LibraryEntryContent` gains `member this.referencedEntryIds : Set<LibraryEntryId>`. For a material it holds the category in `categoryOpt`. For a sample it holds the materials of its payload's structure (`ElementId.fs:SampleStructure.referencedMaterials`), each through `toLibraryEntryId` (step 24). Every other kind references nothing. Its doc says that these are the entries this one names, so that an import never leaves a reference dangling. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, before `CatalogueImportProxy`. Each type and case has a one-line doc citing 001 §B, and the module doc names the table (spec 0050 S3.1). (a) `HeldEntryVersion = { version : VersionNumber; contentHash : ContentHash }` is one version the library holds. `HeldEntry = { id : LibraryEntryId; kind : LibraryEntryKind; name : EntryName; latest : VersionNumber; lifecycle : EntryLifecycle; provenance : EntryProvenance; versions : HeldEntryVersion list }` is what the library holds for one id: the kind, name, lifecycle and provenance of its latest version, and every version, ascending. (b) `ImportOrigin` = `CatalogueImportOrigin of id : CatalogueId * name : CatalogueName` says where the incoming entries come from. (c) `LatestMove` = `MoveLatestVersion` | `KeepLatestVersion`. (d) `ImportAction` = `AddIncomingEntry` | `ReuseHeldEntry` | `AddIncomingVersion of LatestMove` | `ForkIncomingEntry` | `RebindToHeldEntry of LibraryEntryId` | `SkipIncomingEntry` | `RetireHeldEntry`. (e) `ImportStatus` holds the six rows of 001 §B in its order: `EntryIdNotHeld of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope` | `SameContentHash of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * held : HeldEntry` | `VersionNotHeld of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * held : HeldEntry` | `DivergentContent of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * held : HeldEntry` | `NameCollision of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * sameName : HeldEntry list` | `EntryUnlisted of held : HeldEntry`. (g) `ImportDecision = { origin : ImportOrigin; status : ImportStatus; defaultAction : ImportAction; alternatives : ImportAction list }` is one row, and `ImportChoice = { decision : ImportDecision; action : ImportAction }` is a confirmed row. `ImportSplit = { awaiting : ImportDecision list }`; every row requires confirmation. (3) Members of `ImportDecision`. `static member decide (origin : ImportOrigin) (incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope) (heldOpt : HeldEntry option) (sameName : HeldEntry list) : ImportDecision` reads `sameName` (the held entries of the incoming kind and name) only when `heldOpt` is `None`, and applies the rules in this order. A held entry of another kind is `DivergentContent`, because one id cannot name two kinds. A held version equal to the incoming version with an equal hash is `SameContentHash`, defaulting to `ReuseHeldEntry` with no alternative. The same version with another hash is `DivergentContent`, defaulting to `ForkIncomingEntry` with `[ SkipIncomingEntry ]`. A version the entry does not hold is `VersionNotHeld`, defaulting to `AddIncomingVersion move` with `[ SkipIncomingEntry ]`. Here `move` is `MoveLatestVersion` only when the incoming provenance is `BuiltInProvenance c`, the origin is `CatalogueImportOrigin (c, _)`, and the incoming version is above `held.latest`: a protected built-in arriving from its own catalogue (001 §B: 'the local latest moves only for a protected built-in from a catalogue'). Otherwise `move` is `KeepLatestVersion`. Without a held entry, a non-empty `sameName` is `NameCollision`, defaulting to `AddIncomingEntry` (side by side), with one `RebindToHeldEntry` per same-name entry in its order and then `SkipIncomingEntry`. Otherwise the row is `EntryIdNotHeld`, defaulting to `AddIncomingEntry` with `[ SkipIncomingEntry ]`. `static member unlisted (origin : ImportOrigin) (held : HeldEntry) : ImportDecision` is `EntryUnlisted`, defaulting to `RetireHeldEntry` with no alternative. `member this.entryId : LibraryEntryId` and `member this.kind : LibraryEntryKind` read the incoming content, or the held entry for `EntryUnlisted`. `member this.byDefault : ImportChoice` is the row with its default action. `member this.rowName : EntryName` is the name the import dialog shows: the incoming name, or the held name for `EntryUnlisted`. For `NameCollision` it is `<name> — from <catalogue name>` (001 §B 'Si — from A'), a caption only: the entry keeps its own name and hash. `static member split (decisions : ImportDecision list) : ImportSplit` MUST return all decisions in `awaiting`, preserving input order, including `SameContentHash` and independent rows. No store is read, nothing is applied, and no other member is added. (4) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs` (`module ImportDecisionTests`), appended to the compile list after `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` with no comment. Its envelopes come from `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`, and a changed one is sealed through `LibraryEntryContent.sealed` (step 30). Its held entries are test-local `HeldEntry` records built from those envelopes. The origin is `CatalogueImportOrigin (CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue, CatalogueName "Built-in")` unless a fact says otherwise. (a) `a new id is added, or skipped`. (b) `the same id with the same hash is reused and offers nothing else`. (c) `a version not held is added, and only a protected built-in from its own catalogue moves the latest`: Silicon's version 2 under the Built-in origin moves the latest. The same envelope under the origin of a test-local `Lab` catalogue keeps it, as do a user material's version 2 and a built-in version 2 when the held latest is 3. (d) `the same id and version with another hash, or an id held as another kind, is a divergence forked by default`. (e) `a new id with a held entry's name collides, side by side by default, with a re-binding to each held entry`: a `Lab` material named `Silicon` against two held `Silicon` entries offers one `RebindToHeldEntry` for each, in order, and then `SkipIncomingEntry`, and its `rowName` is `Silicon — from Lab`. (f) `an active entry its catalogue no longer lists is retired`. (g) `every decision row awaits confirmation`: `split` of one row per status MUST return all six rows in order. (h) `a row naming an entry that awaits a choice waits with it`: `split` of a colliding category, a new material in that category, a new sample of that material and an unrelated new source MUST answer all four rows as awaiting, in input order. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` gains `an entry's references are its category and its materials`: Silicon's content names exactly its `categoryOpt`'s category, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s names exactly `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial`, and a source names nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the table lands, `CatalogueImport.fs` MUST declare `ImportDecision` with `decide`, `unlisted` and `split`, and no store or caller MUST change; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a new id is added, or skipped`, `the same id with the same hash is reused and offers nothing else`, `a version not held is added, and only a protected built-in from its own catalogue moves the latest`, `the same id and version with another hash, or an id held as another kind, is a divergence forked by default`, `a new id with a held entry's name collides, side by side by default, with a re-binding to each held entry`, `an active entry its catalogue no longer lists is retired`, `every decision row awaits confirmation`, `a row naming an entry that awaits a choice waits with it` and `an entry's references are its category and its materials`, the count rising by 9; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
